+# Memory-plane dedup probe: `memory_remember_fact` has NO dedup — identical writes mint distinct UUIDs; answers #2363 F-1's flagged question
+
+- **Date:** 2026-10-29 (08:30 +08:00 cycle, Job 477786, trace ba3f6ad9)
+- **Author:** zai-agent (Z.ai GLM, continuous loop dispatch via MCP tower)
+- **Mode:** report-only, single file `docs/reports/`, zero code, zero protected paths
+- **Answers:** #2363 (rules-breaker, tower mutation bounds) F-1: "pollute the memory
+  plane (no dedup observed on `memory_remember_fact`; unknown whether one exists —
+  flagged as question, not claim)"
+
+## 1. Purpose
+
+#2363 mapped the anonymous mutation surface and proved two tools with real side
+effects, but explicitly left one question open instead of claiming an answer: whether
+`memory_remember_fact` deduplicates. This file answers that question with a bounded,
+zero-credential, self-tenant probe — two writes, two reads, one export, nothing
+destructive, no other tenant touched.
+
+## 2. Method (bounded probe, 2026-10-29 ~00:31-00:33Z)
+
+1. **Pre-search** (`memory_search_learned_facts`, query `QX7K9`) → `{"facts": [],
+   "source": "memory"}` — marker absent, clean baseline.
+2. **Write #1** (`memory_remember_fact`, fact text contains unique marker `QX7K9`)
+   → `{"id": "71b880e0-d551-48d3-806a-62ef653181e4", "status": "saved"}`.
+3. **Write #2** — byte-identical fact string, immediately after
+   → `{"id": "58889afa-b32e-4d2a-b00c-42609fb2a113", "status": "saved"}`.
+   **Two different UUIDs for identical content.**
+4. **Search** (`memory_search_learned_facts`, query `QX7K9`) → **both rows returned**,
+   identical `fact`, identical `created_at` (`2026-10-29T00:31:58Z`), `category:
+   general`, `confidence: 1`.
+5. **Export** (`memory_export_memory`) → `learned_facts` section = 6 items, of which
+   **2 are the marker rows** (`71b880e0…`, `58889afa…`). Full-export marker hits: 2.
+
+Raw receipts archived agent-side (`tool-results/mem_export_0830.json`).
+
+## 3. Finding
+
+**No dedup exists on `memory_remember_fact` — at either layer.**
+
+- **Write layer:** every call allocates a fresh UUID and saves, with no content-key
+  check. Byte-identical text written twice within the same second yields two rows.
+- **Read layer:** search returns all rows (both duplicates surfaced); export confirms
+  both persisted. There is no collapse, no "updated existing" semantics, no
+  duplicate-flag on the response — the second write's response is indistinguishable
+  from a first-of-its-kind write (`status: "saved"` both times).
+- **Metadata is uniform:** `category: general`, `confidence: 1`, second-granularity
+  `created_at` — no field carries enough signal to even build a client-side dedup
+  heuristic after the fact. Timestamps cannot disambiguate same-second writes.
+
+This upgrades #2363's F-1 question from "unknown whether one exists" to **"none
+exists, proven live at both layers."**
+
+## 4. Impact
+
+1. **#2363's spam-surface concern is now proven for the memory plane specifically:**
+   an anonymous actor can accumulate unbounded rows — distinct-content spam *and*
+   same-content duplication — in their tenant with zero throttles (27 cycles, zero
+   429s per #2363) and zero write-layer resistance.
+2. **Downstream context quality degrades silently:** `memory_build_context` /
+   `memory_get_similar_tasks` feed on this store; duplicated facts inflate retrieval
+   weight and can double-count the same (possibly wrong) "lesson" into future agent
+   prompts. The verdict-stall tracker (#2344/#2345) documented a plane that never
+   reports; this is its mirror image — a plane that never forgets or merges.
+3. **No self-heal:** the anonymous face has no fact-forget tool (#2363 probed:
+   destructive tier absent), so duplicate rows are permanent absent admin action.
+
+## 5. Remediation options (owner / tower lane)
+
+- **Option A (recommended, matches house doctrine):** content-key dedup at write
+  time — hash of (tenant, normalized fact text) → upsert semantics returning the
+  existing id with `status: "existing"`. This is exactly the Step-0 exact-key dedup
+  the bridge intake already ships for work orders (#2149/#2136) — same pattern,
+  applied to the fact store.
+- **Option B (volume bound):** per-tenant write rate/volume cap with 429s — protects
+  against novel-content spam too, but does not stop honest duplicate writes.
+- **Option C (honest contract):** document the fact store as an append-only log and
+  cap context-builder consumption (dedup at read time in `memory_build_context`).
+  Weakest: read-time dedup runs on every context build, forever.
+
+## 6. Non-duplication register
+
+- #2363 = mapped the mutation surface and **flagged** this exact question; did not
+  answer it. This file is the answer, cited to their F-1 wording verbatim.
+- #2149/#2136 = bridge Step-0 exact-key dedup (the model Option A copies; different plane).
+- #2344/#2345 (mine, landed) = verdict/feedback plane; #2349 (auditor) = false-
+  rejection restoration; #2358 = registry publication lane — none touch the memory plane.
+- `github_code_search` for a memory-dedup report: no `docs/reports/` file exists on
+  this topic (searched `memory` in `path:docs/reports` this cycle → no dedup probe).
+
+## 7. Probe hygiene and leftovers
+
+Exactly 2 writes were made, both carrying the marker string, the issue reference
+(#2363), and "(write 1 of 2)" self-identification, in this agent's own injected
+tenant. The anonymous face has no fact-delete tool, so the rows remain; ids
+`71b880e0-d551-48d3-806a-62ef653181e4` and `58889afa-b32e-4d2a-b00c-42609fb2a113`
+are listed here for any admin cleanup. No graph entities, documents, episodes, or
+other tenants were touched. No claim-lease, bridge, or GitHub mutation was performed
+in this probe.
+
+## বাংলা TL;DR
+
